---
import InstallCard from "./InstallCard.astro";
---

<section class="field-guide-home" aria-labelledby="home-heading">
  <InstallCard />
  <p class="section-label">OPERATOR MATH</p>
  <h2 id="home-heading">Start with one simple diagram.</h2>
  <p class="home-intro">
    Find the relationship between chemical feed rate, dose, and flow—then use
    it in any direction. Everything below is the same pie chart, pushed a
    little further.
  </p>

  <a class="featured-reference" href="/operator-math/davidson-pie-chart/">
    <span class="reference-symbol" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 72 72" fill="none">
        <circle cx="36" cy="36" r="31" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
        <path d="M5 36h62" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
        <path d="M36 36 21 63M36 36l15 27" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
        <path d="M5 36A31 31 0 0 1 67 36" fill="currentColor" opacity=".14" />
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span class="reference-copy">
      <span class="reference-type">QUICK REFERENCE</span>
      <strong>Davidson Pie Chart</strong>
      <span>Three worked examples · Feed rate, dose, and flow</span>
    </span>
    <span class="reference-equation" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>dose</span><b>×</b><span>8.34</span><b>×</b><span>flow</span><b>=</b><span>lb/day</span>
    </span>
    <span class="reference-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
  </a>

  <ul class="reference-list">
    <li>
      <a href="/operator-math/three-names/">
        <span class="list-type">DECODER</span>
        <strong>Three Names, One Formula</strong>
        <span class="list-desc">
          Feed rate, loading rate and mass — how to tell which one you were
          handed.
        </span>
        <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/operator-math/demand-strength-purity/">
        <span class="list-type">ADJUSTMENTS</span>
        <strong>Demand, Strength and Purity</strong>
        <span class="list-desc">
          When to subtract before the chart, and when to divide after it.
        </span>
        <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/operator-math/cost-and-supply/">
        <span class="list-type">PLANNING</span>
        <strong>Cost and Days of Supply</strong>
        <span class="list-desc">
          Turning pounds per day into dollars and reorder dates.
        </span>
        <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="home-section">
    <p class="section-label">OPERATOR REFERENCE</p>
    <h2>Look it up, don't memorize it.</h2>
    <p class="home-intro">
      The full formula set, the conversions that feed it, and the twelve pie
      wheels worth keeping in your head — all readable on a phone in the field.
    </p>

    <ul class="reference-list">
      <li>
        <a href="/operator-reference/formulas/">
          <span class="list-type">FORMULAS</span>
          <strong>Formulas</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Every exam formula in US and metric form, grouped by what you're
            working on and filterable by name.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/operator-reference/pie-wheels/">
          <span class="list-type">DIAGRAMS</span>
          <strong>Pie Wheels</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Twelve formulas drawn as wheels — cover the piece you want and read
            off the arithmetic.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/operator-reference/conversion-factors/">
          <span class="list-type">UNITS</span>
          <strong>Conversion Factors</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Get every term into matching units before you run the numbers.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/operator-reference/abbreviations/">
          <span class="list-type">GLOSSARY</span>
          <strong>Abbreviations</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            MLVSS, SSV<sub>30</sub>, SOUR — what the letters on the page
            actually mean.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="home-section">
    <p class="section-label">CALCULATORS</p>
    <h2>Plug in your numbers.</h2>
    <p class="home-intro">
      Calculators that show their work, so the answer comes with the steps
      you'd write on paper.
    </p>

    <ul class="reference-list">
      <li>
        <a href="/calculators/chemical-dosage/">
          <span class="list-type">CHEMICAL FEED</span>
          <strong>Chemical Dosage</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Dose and flow in; lb/day, gal/day and a pump setting in mL/min out.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/calculators/loading-removal/">
          <span class="list-type">LAB RESULTS</span>
          <strong>Loading &amp; Removal</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Pounds per day, removal by stage, organic loading and population equivalent.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/calculators/process-control/">
          <span class="list-type">ACTIVATED SLUDGE</span>
          <strong>Process Control</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            F/M, MCRT, SVI and the WAS rate for a target sludge age.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/calculators/clarifier-loading/">
          <span class="list-type">CLARIFIERS</span>
          <strong>Clarifier &amp; Tank Loading</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Detention time, surface and weir overflow and solids loading, checked against typical ranges.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/calculators/pipe-flow/">
          <span class="list-type">COLLECTION</span>
          <strong>Pipe Flow</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Full-pipe velocity, partly full sewers with Manning, and force main head loss.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/calculators/stank-index/">
          <span class="list-type">JUST FOR FUN</span>
          <strong>Stank Index</strong>
          <span class="list-desc">
            Pounds of stank per day, nose-blind time and break room clearance. Totally made up.
          </span>
          <span class="list-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</section>

<style>
  .field-guide-home {
    --ink: var(--fg-ink);
    --muted: var(--fg-muted);
    --teal: var(--fg-teal);
    --line: var(--fg-line);

    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: 1.25rem auto 0;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem) clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem) 2rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--fg-font);
  }

  .section-label,
  .reference-type {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    color: #0f877c;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  }

  .field-guide-home h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .home-intro {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.12rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .featured-reference {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(14rem, 1fr) auto auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: #fff;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;
  }

  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .featured-reference {
    background: #1b2a32;
  }

  .featured-reference:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: #9ecdc9;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgb(20 58 73 / 9%);
  }

  .featured-reference:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #168f85;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .reference-symbol {
    display: grid;
    width: 3.75rem;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 0.9rem;
    background: #eaf6f5;
    color: var(--teal);
  }

  .reference-symbol svg {
    width: 2.5rem;
  }

  .reference-copy {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: start;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .reference-type {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  }

  .reference-copy strong {
    font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 2vw, 1.3rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .reference-copy > span:last-child {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .reference-equation {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    color: #236f9b;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .reference-equation {
    color: #9bd6f1;
  }

  .reference-equation b {
    color: #8497a2;
  }

  .reference-arrow {
    color: #128c82;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .home-section {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .home-section .home-intro {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .reference-list > :global(*) {
    /* Starlight's markdown flow adds margin-top to every sibling, which staggers grid rows. */
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .reference-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .reference-list a {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: #fff;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease, box-shadow 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease;
  }

  :global(html[data-theme="dark"]) .reference-list a {
    background: #1b2a32;
  }

  .reference-list a:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: #9ecdc9;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgb(20 58 73 / 9%);
  }

  .reference-list a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid #168f85;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  .list-type {
    color: #0f877c;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  }

  .reference-list strong {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .list-desc {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .list-type,
  .reference-list strong,
  .list-desc {
    grid-column: 1;
  }

  .list-arrow {
    grid-row: 1 / 3;
    grid-column: 2;
    color: #128c82;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .field-guide-home {
      padding-inline: 0.25rem;
    }

    .featured-reference {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      gap: 0.9rem;
    }

    .reference-equation {
      grid-column: 2 / 3;
      justify-content: flex-start;
    }

    .reference-arrow {
      grid-column: 3;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .featured-reference,
    .reference-list a {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
